        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-08T19:48:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The alternatives are:\n\n1. Keep `SkGetJpegInfo` and add an icc output parameter. The implementation in `SkJpegInfo_libjpegturbo.cpp` could be updated to use `SkCodec` (as is done here) and `SkJpegInfo_none.cpp` could be updated to parse out the icc profile or just return nullptr. Just extending this existing solution has the downside of being a build selected alternate which we are trying to get away from.\n\n2. Do what is right here, just make pdf always depend on `SkJpegDecoder`. It appears all current users of pdf also depend on this codec anyway. However, it is a little awkward if the user doesn\u0027t otherwise need a jpeg decoder or has their own.\n\n3. Allow a `SkCodecs::Decoder` to be passed in (on `Metadata`?). This is awkward because it would need to be a jpeg decoder (or at least a jpeg header decoder) and not something else, otherwise very surprising things might happen. Also, if they don\u0027t pass one in (which may be easy to miss) then this optimization can\u0027t happen, and it is fairly important.",
      "parentUuid": "35bcc65f_cc1d4462",
      "revId": "4f48f994d2b15dd9075eb0d818e1ade17b8e7961",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
